From 9197c56d49d21a28ce0c47fd5a6dbb43467e40ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:58:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: progress bar and update log on the updater page

- A row at the top of the page shows the phase (copy, verify, install,
  validate, finalize, done, failed), a progress bar with the percentage, a
  short note on what the phase does and the last lines of the update log;
  tapping it opens the whole log (copy, clear)
- The log (device-protected storage, about 96 KB, also logcat UpdaterLog)
  records the file, signature and metadata checks, the update's source and
  target build, every update_engine status change and each 10% within it,
  the result by name, and the build and slot after the restart

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VXjYUWzBqMCeUoJD2Suc4
